A||||20||Cheever2||Do you have a favorite glass, cup or mug?||||10||
Z||000000||Cheever2||05-16-2001||02:46 PM||||Mine is nothing special, just a green Coke glass with the bumpy texture.  It's the right size & shape for carrying around ice tea or Coke.  I also like my Indy 500 mug, and my mug from the Neil Armstrong Museum in SW Ohio (I used to live 5 miles from Neil).<P>Of course, I am often caught in the middle of the night drinking directly from a jug or pitcher.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-16-2001||02:54 PM||||My favorite cup is a can of coke! And no you can't pour it in a glass, and no it doesn't taste the same in the bottle!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||05-16-2001||03:07 PM||||You guys are after my own heart with your stories of Coke.  I drink my Diet Coke from a pink plastic "glass".  I got it 25 years ago on June 5th on my way to my bachelor party.  It was the Sat before our wedding on June 12th.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||05-16-2001||03:24 PM||||Heck ya!!!  My Fiero coffee mug I got from <B>Alex</B>!!!<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002402.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/002402.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||FieroLisa||05-16-2001||03:27 PM||||Speaking of glasses...the last car show I went to in Indianapolis gave away some cool trophies..I won 2nd place and got an etched water glass thats pretty cool, says the name of the show, Fiero Class & second place. But I doubt I'll ever drink from it, it just sits around looking pretty and collecting dust.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||05-16-2001||03:31 PM||||Depends on what I'm drinking.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Actually, I have some nice pub mugs I prefer for my malted beverages.  I have a set of special 6oz, 6" tall shot glasses for when times call for drastic measures.  I have a couple of old style pilsner glasses from the Kanki at Crabtree Valley mall before they renovated.  They got rid of all the old glasses.  Some fun times were had in the old upstairs bar, which doesn't exist anymore.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>So I really don't have one favorite glass, but depending on what I'm drinking, I do have a favorite for that type of beverage.  Another of my favorites is my Kenny shot glass from South Park.  Nothing special until I turned on the garbage disposal one day and the vibration caused it to slide off the counter and into the garbage disposal!  Now my Kenney shot glass has a big crack and chip of glass missing right over his head!  It's TOO perfect!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   That, and everytime you do a shot, "you killed Kenny." ||||reg||6
Z||000006||loafer87gt||05-16-2001||03:40 PM||||Plastic beer cups all the way. Other than that my favorite mug is the Schooner mug I 'borrowed' from Boston Pizza. It can hold three and a half beers.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jay||05-16-2001||04:40 PM||||My favorite is a tall frosted glass that has "The Sopranos" etched in it on one side and "Bada Bing" on the other with one of those silhouette stripper chicks on it.  I've got two of them just in case one breaks.  And yes it is big enough to fit a can and a half of Coke in it.  Pepsi will never see that glass!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> BTW I prefere Coke in a bottle rather than a can.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
Z||000008||saleenfiero||05-16-2001||04:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Plastic beer cups all the way. Other than that my favorite mug is the Schooner mug I 'borrowed' from Boston Pizza. It can hold three and a half beers.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You should try scamming one of the party pitchers, those are much more fun than a schooner (although I don't usually drink beer from anything else other than a schooner!)<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||05-16-2001||05:49 PM||||I have a coffee cup in my office that's made like a pyrex laboratory beaker. <BR>It was a gift from my wife, the chemistry geek.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>It even has a graduated milliliter scale on the side. <BR>Really weirds out some of the folks I work with. I told one of the more squeamish folks to imagine me drinking apple juice from it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||JSocha||05-16-2001||06:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Plastic beer cups all the way. Other than that my favorite mug is the Schooner mug I 'borrowed' from Boston Pizza. It can hold three and a half beers.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A 5 gallon pail.  My wife tells me when we go out to street dances where drinking is always involved that "I am only allowed to have one drink".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Have to make the most with the least!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Taijiguy||05-16-2001||07:40 PM||||Two favorite mugs:<BR>One from Dunoon ceramics with the name of the sub I served on: USS Andrew Jackson SSBN 619<BR>My "Far Side" mug with the picture of a kid pushing on a door that says "Pull" with a sign in front about a school for the gifted.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||05-16-2001||09:26 PM||||I have some of the Coke "freezer mugs" that have that weird blue gel in them to keep my cola cold. If my wife would leave them alone and in the freezer, my marriage would probably be much happier  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||05-17-2001||12:20 PM||||Hmmmm... wow, this post really made me take a look at just how 'into' "drinking propriety" I must be...  or I just have lots of glassware and I like to use it 'cuz it's neat.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If I'm drinking Killian's Red (my standard), I'll drink it out of one of the six KR pub pint glasses I have, or the .5 litre ceramic KR stein I picked up on eBay. <P>If I'm drinking Weeping Radish beer (no, there are no radishes in it - it's the name of the brewery/pub, and it's my all-time favorite), then I'll usually use either my tall glass WR .5 litre stein or the cobalt blue stoneware WR mug, or one of the .5 litre WR Beer Club Member's steins I have. <P>If I'm drinking wine, I'll use one of a pair of gold-rimmed crystal wineglasses...<P>If I'm drinking hard liquor or plum wine, I'll use a 7"-tall (but standard diameter) shot glasses (as seen in Londo Mollari's hand on the Babylon 5 sci-fi TV series).<P>If I'm drinking anything else at home, it usually goes in one of my cobalt blue glass pint glasses. <P>If I drink coffee at home, it goes in the black coffee mug I got from Space Camp in Huntsville, AL. If it's coffee on the go, it's usually in an oversized travel mug from Breugger's Bagel Bakery.<P>If I'm at a RenFaire in garb, I use a pewter chalice for whatever I happen to be drinking. If I'm at a RenFaire in standard streetclothes, I use either the ceramic stein I got from the Minneapolis RenFaire a few years ago, or the ceramic pilsner glass I got from the Carolina RenFaire last year (each with the corresponding RenFaire logo cast on the side).<P><BR>Man... talk about obsessive!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>EDIT: typos and smiley-fixin'... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cheever2||05-17-2001||02:02 PM||||Wow.<P>LZeit, you shoulda started this thread yourself a long time ago!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000015||LZeitgeist||05-17-2001||03:33 PM||||"Hi... my name is LZeitgeist, and I have a drinking problem..."<P>"Hi, LZeitgeist!"<P>"No, not *that* kind of drinking problem... I can't figure out what kind of glass I'm supposed to use for milk... I don't have a milk-specific glass yet..."||||reg||1
